  "adapter_rules": [
    "All cases start from the declared fresh three-member policy. reserve is a durable unique canonical reservation; apply/append_attempt require that original reservation. A runtime hook must perform these steps together before effects, not offer an unreserved bypass.",
    "repeat expands the indicated exact action count. Every repeated append_attempt charges its actual canonical bytes+13+(12 if digest present), even a later failed I/O; failure cannot refund. A denied pure transition leaves state unchanged.",
    "canonicalBytesOverride tests stored-map size conflict; original checked canonical witness bytes/hash remain those of the referenced record. No substitute quota is accepted.",
    "restart_roundtrip means persist/reload equivalent complete state, not a new lease. No serialized coordinator storage format is selected by this corpus.",
    "Generation deduplication is per (member,exact filename). It does not authorize concurrent physical reincarnations/old unlinked-inode overlap or replace file-extent admission.",
    "Semantic record decoding, exact resolved operands, immutable-byte tokens, trusted bootstrap/import lineage, atomic coordinator durability and source hook coverage are separate required integration premises. Root SetData wire inputs here are small/large arithmetic fixtures, not a native producer schema."
  ]
}
